# OpenSpec git (standing authorization)

While working on a named OpenSpec change, do not wait for a second “please commit”.

| Unit | Git |
| --- | --- |
| Change `<name>` | Worktree `.worktrees/<name>` on branch `change/<name>` — never `main` |
| One `tasks.md` checkbox | One Conventional Commit (include the `- [x]`) |
| All apply tasks done | `git push` and `gh pr create` targeting `main` |

- Add or reuse that worktree before propose, update, apply, or archive. Keep the primary checkout on `main`.
- After creating or selecting the worktree, call `move_agent_to_root` on its absolute path before any edits.
- Reuse the existing worktree/branch for that change. Stop if the hub tree has unrelated dirty files.
- Do not batch tasks. Do not merge the PR unless asked. Do not `git worktree remove` unless asked.
- Propose/update: one commit when that planning pass is complete. Archive: one commit, then push to update the PR.
- Typo/comment work that skips OpenSpec still needs an explicit commit request.

Full protocol: `AGENTS.md` section **Git for OpenSpec changes**.
